simrad.AR: Implementation of a radar emulator in WRF

L. Fita, V. Galligani (CIMA-IFAECI), Aregntina

This effort is absolutely in shoulders of giants and is based in multiple different works:

 - Bessel, F. W., (1826) On the computation of geographical longitude and latitude from geodetic measurements, Astronomische Nachrichten (Astronomical Notes), Band 4, No. 86, Spalten 241-254, Altona 1826
 - Leinonen, J., High-level interface to T-matrix scattering calculations: architecture, capabilities and limitations, Opt. Express, vol. 22, issue 2, 1655-1660 (2014), doi: 10.1364/OE.22.001655.
 - Mishchenko, M. I. and L. D. Travis, T-matrix computations of light scattering by large spheroidal particles, Opt. Commun., vol. 109, 16-21 (1994)
 - Mishchenko, M. I., L. D. Travis, and A. Macke, Scattering of light by polydisperse, randomly oriented, finite circular cylinders, Appl. Opt., vol. 35, 4927-4940 (1996)
 - Vincenty, T., (1975) Direct and inverse solutions on the ellipsoid with application of nested equations, Survey Review, Vol. 23, No. 176, pp. 88-93.
 - Vincenty, T., (1976) Correspondence: solutions of geodesics, survey Review, Vol. 23, No. 180, p. 294.
 - Wielaard, D. J., M. I. Mishchenko, A. Macke, and B. E. Carlson, Improved T-matrix computations for large, nonabsorbing and weakly absorbing nonspherical particles and comparison with geometrical optics approximation, Appl. Opt., vol. 36, 4305-4313 (1997)


There is a prototype off-line working version available from CIMA's GIT repository, from which the code is based on:
https://git.cima.fcen.uba.ar/lluis.fita/simradar/-/wikis/home

This code is available from Lluis Fita's WRF fork (git@github.com:LluisFB/WRF.git) in branch 'simradAR'

== Usage ==
A new section into the WRF's namelist calles 'simradar' has to be set up

=== namelist ===
simradar&
/

| type     | name                | default value       | description                                                         | units |
| ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- |
| integer   | nradar              | 1                   | amount of surface radar                                            | # |
| integer   | e_dist              | 800                 | radar grid points along the radii [computed as                     | # |
|           |                     |                     |    2.*max(distmax) / min(radards)]                                 | # |
| integer   | e_angle             | 376                 | radar amount of horizontal angles  [computed as                    | # |
|           |                     |                     |    2*pi*radii_ddist / (min(ddist))                                 | # |
| integer   | e_azimuth           | 15                  | radar amount of azimuths (vertical angle) [same for all radars]    | # |
| integer   | ngrid_radar         | 1500                | maximum amount of radar cells into a given WRF grid point          | # |
| integer   | ngrid3_radar        | 25000               | maximum amount of vertical radar cells into a given WRF grid point | # | 
| integer   | nradar_ngrid        | 30000               | nradar*ngrid_radar                                                 | # |
| integer   | nradar_ngrid_coord2 | 60000               | nradar_ngrid_coord2                                                | # |
| integer   | nradar_coord2       | 40                  | nradar*coord2                                                      | # |
| integer   | nradar_coord4       | 160                 | nradar*coord4                                                      | # |
| integer   | ngrid_coord2        | 60000               | ngrid_radar*coord2                                                 | # |
| integer   | nradar_azimuth      | 300                 | nradar*e_azimuth                                                   | # |
| integer   | nradar_dist         | 1600                | nradar*e_dist                                                      | # |
| integer   | Nbands              | 3                   | amount of radar bands                                              | # |
| integer   | Nluticebins         | 200                 | amount of ice bins for LUT interpolations                          | # |
| integer   | Nlutqxbins          | 50000               | amount of water species bins for LUT interpolations                | # |
| integer   | Nlutlevs            | 15                  | amount of azimuths for LUT interpolations                          | # |
| character | radar_name          | '-'                 | name of the radar [one per radar]                                  | - |
| real      | radar_clon          | 0.0                 | longitude of the location of the radar    [one per radar]          | degree_east  |
| real      | radar_clat          | 0.0                 | latitude of the location of the radar [one per radar]              | degree_north |
| real      | radar_chgt          | 0.0                 | height of the location of the radar  [one per radar]               | m |
| character | radar_band          | '-'                 | band of the radar: 'c', 's', or 'x'  [one per radar]               | - |
| integer   | radar_scan          | 1                   | type of scan 1:             [one per radar]                        | - |
| real      | radar_distmax       | 250.                | maximum distance from radar [one per radar]                        | km |
| real      | radar_hgtmax        | 20.                 | maximum height from radar  [one per radar]                         | km |
| integer   | em_ray              | 1                   | type of propagation of em ray. 1: 4/3 Ref [one per radar]          | - |
|           |                     |                     |      1:     4/3 Ref                                                |   |
| real      | radards             | 250.                | nominal horizontal resolution of radar values [one per radar]      | m |
| integer   | radinterp           | 1                   | method of interpolation to the radar space (1: inverted distance weighted) | - |
| real      | radii_dist          | 15.                 | radii at which arc resolution is the same as minimum radards       | km |
| integer   | eloption            | 1                   | Ellipsoide                                                         | - |
|           |                     |                     |      1: 'GRS80 / WGS84  (NAD83)'                                   |   |
|           |                     |                     |        a = 6378137.d0                                              |   |
|           |                     |                     |        f = 1.d0/298.25722210088d0                                  |   |
|           |                     |                     |      2: 'Clarke 1866    (NAD27)'                                   |   |
|           |                     |                     |        a = 6378206.4d0                                             |   |
|           |                     |                     |        f = 1.d0/294.9786982138d0                                   |   |
| real      | missing_value       | 1.e20               | missing value                                                      | - |
| integer   | doppler_scheme      | 1                   | method to compute the doppler velocities                           | - |
|           |                     |                     |   0: Reflectivity weighted terminal velocity                       |   |
|           |                     |                     |   1: Get PSD integrated backscattering cross section int = v S/S   |   |
|           |                     |                     |      [not implemented]                                             |   |
| integer   | timedbg             | 720                 | frecuency of time-debugging                                        | minute |
| real      | londbg              | -999.               | longitude of grid-point debugging (-999., not used)                | degree_east  |
| real      | latdbg              | -999.               | latitude of grid-point debugging (-999., not used)                 | degree_north |
| character | lutfilen            | TMATRIX_WRF_WSM6.nc | name of the netCDF file with the T-Matrix lool-up-tables           | - |
| real      | q_rain_min          | 1e-7                | minimum rain mixing ratio to consider                              | kgkg-1" |
| real      | q_rain_max          | 0.02                | maximum rain mixing ratio to consider                              | kgkg-1 |
| real      | qn_rain_min         | 1e-8                | minimum amount of nuclii for rain to consider                      | # |
| real      | qn_rain_max         | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for rain to consider                      | # |
| real      | q_snow_min          | 1e-7                | minimum snow mixing ratio to consider                              | kgkg-1 |
| real      | q_snow_max          | 0.018               | maximum snow mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| real      | qn_snow_min         | 1e-7                | minimum amount of nuclii for snow to consider"                     | # |
| real      | qn_snow_max         | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for snow to consider"                     | # |
| real      | q_grau_min          | 1e-7                | minimum grau mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| real      | q_grau_max          | 0.018               | maximum grau mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| real      | qn_grau_min         | 1E-7                | minimum amount of nuclii for grau to consider"                     | # |
| real      | qn_grau_max         | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for grau to consider"                     | # |
| real      | q_ice_min           | 1e-7                | minimum cloud ice mixing ratio to consider"                        | kgkg-1 |
| real      | q_ice_max           | 0.001               | maximum cloud ice mixing ratio to consider"                        | kgkg-1 |
| real      | qn_ice_min          | 1e-8                | minimum amount of nuclii for cloud ice to consider"                | # |
| real      | qn_ice_max          | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for cloud ice to consider"                | # |
| real      | q_hail_min          | -9999.              | minimum hail mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| real      | q_hail_max          | -9999.              | maximum hail mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| real      | qn_hail_min         | -9999.              | minimum amount of nuclii for hail to consider"                     | # |
| real      | qn_hail_max         | -9999.              | maximum amount of nuclii for hail to consider"                     | # |
| real      | q_clou_min          | 1e-10               | minimum clou mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| real      | q_clou_max          | 0.013               | maximum clou mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
| integer   | dim_ice             | 200                 | dimension for ice bins"                                            | - |
| integer   | Nqxbins             | 50000               | dimension for water species bins"                                  | - |

Output is expected at the 11th auxiliary history output, therefore standard set-up for the output is expected in the history section of the namelist

 auxhist11_outname = "wrfsimradar_d<domain>_<date>"
 auxhist11_interval = 10, 10,
 frames_per_auxhist11 = 6, 6,
 io_form_auxhist11 = 2

=== LUT values ===
A series of look-up tables have to be prepared for each different microphysics scheme. There,via the use of the T-matrix method, conversion of mixing ratio values for each species are computed. All this information has to be prepared in advance and kept in a netCDF file.

For example, the structure of the file for the WSM6 microphsyics looks like:

$ ncdump -h TMATRIX_WRF_WSM6.nc 

netcdf TMATRIX_WRF_WSM6 {
dimensions:
        radar_band = 3 ;
        elevation = 15 ;
        frequency = 50000 ;
        C1 = 1 ;
        StringLength = 256 ;
variables:
        char radar_band(radar_band, C1) ;
                radar_band:standard_name = "band" ;
                radar_band:long_name = "band of the radar" ;
                radar_band:units = "-" ;
        float elevation(elevation) ;
                elevation:standard_name = "elevation" ;
                elevation:long_name = "vertical angle of elevation (azimuth)" ;
                elevation:units = "degree" ;
        char WRF_mp_physics(StringLength) ;
                WRF_mp_physics:standard_name = "microphysics" ;
                WRF_mp_physics:long_name = "name of the microphysics scheme from WRF" ;
                WRF_mp_physics:units = "-" ;
        float q_rain_min ;
        float q_rain_max ;
        float qn_rain_min ;
        float qn_rain_max ;
        float q_snow_min ;
        float q_snow_max ;
        float qn_snow_min ;
        float qn_snow_max ;
        float q_grau_min ;
        float q_grau_max ;
        float qn_grau_min ;
        float qn_grau_max ;
        float q_ice_min ;
        float q_ice_max ;
        float qn_ice_min ;
        float qn_ice_max ;
        float q_clou_min ;
        float q_clou_max ;
        int dim_ice ;
        int dimv ;
        float rhoo ;
        float rho_r ;
        float n0r ;
        float rho_s ;
        float n0s ;
        float rho_g ;
        float n0g ;
        float rho_h ;
        float n0h ;
        double Zh_RAIN(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zh_RAIN:standard_name = "Zh_RAIN" ;
                Zh_RAIN:long_name = "Zh for RAIN" ;
                Zh_RAIN:units = "-" ;
        double Zh_SNOW(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zh_SNOW:standard_name = "Zh_SNOW" ;
                Zh_SNOW:long_name = "Zh for SNOW" ;
                Zh_SNOW:units = "-" ;
        double Zh_GRAU(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zh_GRAU:standard_name = "Zh_GRAU" ;
                Zh_GRAU:long_name = "Zh for GRAU" ;
                Zh_GRAU:units = "-" ;
        double Zh_ICE(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zh_ICE:standard_name = "Zh_ICE" ;
                Zh_ICE:long_name = "Zh for ICE" ;
                Zh_ICE:units = "-" ;
        double Zdr_RAIN(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zdr_RAIN:standard_name = "Zdr_RAIN" ;
                Zdr_RAIN:long_name = "Zdr for RAIN" ;
                Zdr_RAIN:units = "-" ;
        double Zdr_SNOW(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zdr_SNOW:standard_name = "Zdr_SNOW" ;
                Zdr_SNOW:long_name = "Zdr for SNOW" ;
                Zdr_SNOW:units = "-" ;
        double Zdr_GRAU(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zdr_GRAU:standard_name = "Zdr_GRAU" ;
                Zdr_GRAU:long_name = "Zdr for GRAU" ;
                Zdr_GRAU:units = "-" ;
        double Zdr_ICE(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Zdr_ICE:standard_name = "Zdr_ICE" ;
                Zdr_ICE:long_name = "Zdr for ICE" ;
                Zdr_ICE:units = "-" ;
        double LDR_RAIN(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                LDR_RAIN:standard_name = "LDR_RAIN" ;
                LDR_RAIN:long_name = "LDR for RAIN" ;
                LDR_RAIN:units = "-" ;
        double LDR_SNOW(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                LDR_SNOW:standard_name = "LDR_SNOW" ;
                LDR_SNOW:long_name = "LDR for SNOW" ;
                LDR_SNOW:units = "-" ;
        double LDR_GRAU(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                LDR_GRAU:standard_name = "LDR_GRAU" ;
                LDR_GRAU:long_name = "LDR for GRAU" ;
                LDR_GRAU:units = "-" ;
        double LDR_ICE(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                LDR_ICE:standard_name = "LDR_ICE" ;
                LDR_ICE:long_name = "LDR for ICE" ;
                LDR_ICE:units = "-" ;
        double Aih_RAIN(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aih_RAIN:standard_name = "Aih_RAIN" ;
                Aih_RAIN:long_name = "Aih for RAIN" ;
                Aih_RAIN:units = "-" ;
        double Aih_SNOW(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aih_SNOW:standard_name = "Aih_SNOW" ;
                Aih_SNOW:long_name = "Aih for SNOW" ;
                Aih_SNOW:units = "-" ;
        double Aih_GRAU(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aih_GRAU:standard_name = "Aih_GRAU" ;
                Aih_GRAU:long_name = "Aih for GRAU" ;
                Aih_GRAU:units = "-" ;
        double Aih_ICE(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aih_ICE:standard_name = "Aih_ICE" ;
                Aih_ICE:long_name = "Aih for ICE" ;
                Aih_ICE:units = "-" ;
        double Aiv_RAIN(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aiv_RAIN:standard_name = "Aiv_RAIN" ;
                Aiv_RAIN:long_name = "Aiv for RAIN" ;
                Aiv_RAIN:units = "-" ;
        double Aiv_SNOW(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aiv_SNOW:standard_name = "Aiv_SNOW" ;
                Aiv_SNOW:long_name = "Aiv for SNOW" ;
                Aiv_SNOW:units = "-" ;
        double Aiv_GRAU(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aiv_GRAU:standard_name = "Aiv_GRAU" ;
                Aiv_GRAU:long_name = "Aiv for GRAU" ;
                Aiv_GRAU:units = "-" ;
        double Aiv_ICE(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                Aiv_ICE:standard_name = "Aiv_ICE" ;
                Aiv_ICE:long_name = "Aiv for ICE" ;
                Aiv_ICE:units = "-" ;
        double KDP_RAIN(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                KDP_RAIN:standard_name = "KDP_RAIN" ;
                KDP_RAIN:long_name = "KDP for RAIN" ;
                KDP_RAIN:units = "-" ;
        double KDP_SNOW(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                KDP_SNOW:standard_name = "KDP_SNOW" ;
                KDP_SNOW:long_name = "KDP for SNOW" ;
                KDP_SNOW:units = "-" ;
        double KDP_GRAU(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                KDP_GRAU:standard_name = "KDP_GRAU" ;
                KDP_GRAU:long_name = "KDP for GRAU" ;
                KDP_GRAU:units = "-" ;
        double KDP_ICE(frequency, elevation, radar_band) ;
                KDP_ICE:standard_name = "KDP_ICE" ;
                KDP_ICE:long_name = "KDP for ICE" ;
                KDP_ICE:units = "-" ;

// global attributes:
                :project = "simrad.AR: radar emulator for WRF" ;
                :reference1 = "Leinonen, J., High-level interface to T-matrix scattering calculations: architecture, capabilities and limitations, Opt. Express, vol. 22, issue 2, 1655-1660 (2014), doi: 10.1364/OE.22.001655." ;
                :reference2 = "Mishchenko, M. I. and L. D. Travis, T-matrix computations of light scattering by large spheroidal particles, Opt. Commun., vol. 109, 16-21 (1994)" ;
                :reference3 = "Mishchenko, M. I., L. D. Travis, and A. Macke, Scattering of light by polydisperse, randomly oriented, finite circular cylinders, Appl. Opt., vol. 35, 4927-4940 (1996)" ;
                :reference4 = "Wielaard, D. J., M. I. Mishchenko, A. Macke, and B. E. Carlson, Improved T-matrix computations for large, nonabsorbing and weakly absorbing nonspherical particles and comparison with geometrical optics  approximation, Appl. Opt., vol. 36, 4305-4313 (1997)" ;
                :file_description = "T-matrix derived light scattering values for WRF\'s microphysic parametrization WSM6" ;
                :file_author = "Vito Galligani" ;
                :file_institution1 = "Centro de Investigaciones del Mar y la Atmosfera (CIMA)" ;
                :file_institution2 = "Instituto Franco-Argentino sobre Estudios de Clima y sus Impactos (UBA-CONICET-CNRS-IRD, IRL-3351-IFAECI)" ;
                :file_version = "1" ;
                :file_date = "January 2026" ;

This file has to be in the WRF/run folder in order to be read and taken into consideration

== Output ==
Accordingly to thge set-up provided for auxhist11, the specific file will contain the following variables
| type    | name            | dimensions                                  | description                                                 | units |
| integer | ijraddbg        | iit                                         | i,j-grid points from londbg,latdbg for simrad.AR debugging  | - |
| integer | inradar         | west_east, south_north                      | pertinence of the grid cell to any radar (1: yes)           | 1 |
| integer | radarnum        | west_east, south_north, nradar              | pertinence of the grid cell inside a given radar area       | 1 |
| real    | RADARS_DIST     | e_dist, nradar                              | ground radar gate distances to their center                 | m |
| real    | RADARS_ANGLE    | e_angle, nradar                             | ground radar gate horizontal angles to emit beams           | m |
| real    | RADARS_AZIMUTH  | e_angle, nradar                             | ground radar gate vertical angles to emit beams             | m |
| real    | RADARLONS       | e_angle, e_dist, nradar                     | ground radar gate longitude                                 | degree_east |
| real    | RADARLATS       | e_angle, e_dist, nradar                     | ground radar gate latitude                                  | degree_north |
| real    | RADARHGTS       | e_azimuth, e_dist, nradar                   | ground radar gate height                                    | m |
| real    | RADARLHGTS      | e_azimuth, e_dist, nradar                   | ground radar gate local height                              | m |
| real    | RADARDIST       | e_angle, e_dist, nradar                     | ground radar horizontal distance of the grid point          | m |
| real    | RADARLON_BNDS   | e_angle, e_dist, nradar_coord4              | ground radar gate longitude bounds                          | degree_east |
| real    | RADARLAT_BNDS   | e_angle, e_dist, nradar_coord4              | ground radar gate latitude bounds                           | degree_north |
| real    | RADARHGT_BNDS   | e_azimuth, e_dist, nradar_coord4            | ground radar gate height bounds                             | m |
| real    | GATEHDIST       | west_east, south_north, nradar              | distacnce of the grid points to the position of the radar   | m |
| integer | NGRIDRADAR      | west_east, south_north, nradar              | amount of radar cells inside the grid point                 | 1 |
| integer | IJGRIDRADAR     | west_east, south_north, nradar_ngrid_coord2 | coordinates of radar cells inside the grid point            | - |
| real    | IJDISTGRIDRADAR | west_east, south_north, nradar_ngrid        | distance of radar cells inside the grid point to its center | m |
| real    | ZH_RAIN         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Reflectivity for Rain                                       | dBz |
| real    | ZDR_RAIN        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | ZDR for Rain                                                | dBz |
| real    | KDP_RAIN        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | KDP for Rain                                                | degree/km |
| real    | ZH_SNOW         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Reflectivity for Snow                                       | dBz |
| real    | ZDR_SNOW        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | ZDR for Snow                                                | dBz |
| real    | KDP_SNOW        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | KDP for Snow                                                | degree/km |
| real    | ZH_GRAU         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Reflectivity for Graupel                                    | dBz |
| real    | ZDR_GRAU        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | ZDR for Graupel                                             | dBz |
| real    | KDP_GRAU        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | KDP for Graupel                                             | degree/km |
| real    | ZH_ICE          | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Reflectivity for cloud Ice                                  | dBz |
| real    | ZDR_ICE         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | ZDR for cloud Ice                                           | dBz |
| real    | KDP_ICE         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | KDP for cloud Ice                                           | degree/km |
| real    | ZH_HAIL         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Reflectivity for Hail                                       | dBz |
| real    | ZDR_HAIL        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | ZDR for Hail                                                | dBz |
| real    | KDP_HAIL        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | KDP for Hail                                                | degree/km |
| real    | ZH_TOTAL        | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Reflectivity for all species                                | dBz |
| real    | ZDR_TOTAL       | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | ZDR for all species                                         | dBz |
| real    | KDP_TOTAL       | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | KDP for all species                                         | degree/km |
| real    | TV_RAIN         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | terminal velocity for Rain                                  | ms-1 |
| real    | TV_SNOW         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | terminal velocity for Snow                                  | ms-1 |
| real    | TV_GRAU         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | terminal velocity for Graupel                               | ms-1 |
| real    | TV_ICE          | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | terminal velocity for cloud Ice                             | ms-1 |
| real    | TV_HAIL         | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | terminal velocity for Hail                                  | ms-1 |
| real    | TV_WGT          | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | weighted terminal velocity                                  | ms-1 |
| real    | VR              | e_angle, e_azimuth, nradar_dist             | Doppler velocity                                            | ms-1 |

NOTE:
 WRF can not provide 5-dimensional output variables. Here amount of radars and vertical coordinate are collapsed into different dimensions, therefore outputs will be
    IJDISTGRIDRADAR(e_we,e_sn,nradar_ngrid,Time) therefore it will be needed to decompress the nradar, ngrid_radar dimensions IJDISTGRIDRADAR(e_we,e_sn,ngrid_radar,nradar,Time)
    IJGRIDRADAR(e_we,e_sn,nradar_ngrid_coord2,Time) --> IJGRIDRADAR(e_we,e_sn,ngrid_radar,coord2,nradar,Time)
    RADARLON_BNDS(e_angle,e_dist,nradar_coord4,Time) --> RADARLON_BNDS(e_angle,e_dist,coord4,nradar,Time)
    RADARLAT_BNDS(e_angle,e_dist,nradar_coord4,Time) --> RADARLAT_BNDS(e_angle,e_dist,coord4,nradar,Time)
    RADARHGT_BNDS(e_azimuth,e_dist,nradar_coord4,Time) --> RADARHGT_BNDS(e_azimuth,e_dist,coord4,nradar,Time)
    ZH_RAIN(e_angle,e_azimuth,nradar_dist,Time) --> RADARHGT_BNDS(e_angle,e_azimuth,e_dist,nradar,Time)
  For example:
  DO ia=1, e_angle
    DO id=1, e_dist
      DO ir=1, nradar
        DO j=1, coord4
          irj = (ir-1)*coord4 + j
          radarlon_bnds(ia,id,irj) = lon_bnds(ia,id,j,ir)
        END DO
      END DO
    END DO
  END DO


== Installation ==

1.- Get the repository from a $WORKDIR
git clone git@github.com:LluisFB/WRF.git

2.- getting submoules
git submodule update --init --recursive

3.- Switching to the simrad.AR branch
git checkout simradAR

4.- Preparing installation (remember to define WRFIO_NCD_LARGE_FILE_SUPPORT=1 and NETCDF)
./configure

5.- Editing configure.wrf to add -DSIMRADAR pre-compilation flag
cp configure.wrf configure.simradAR.orig
cp configure.wrf configure.simradAR.wrf
vim configure.simradAR.wrf
diff configure.wrf.orig configure.simradAR.wrf
216c216
<                        \
---
>                       -DSIMRADAR \
cp configure.simradAR.wrf configure.wrf

6.- Compile as usual
./compile em_real >& compile.log



